Explanation of the change:

- We pull the conditional expansion/collapse logic into a `useEffect` that listens to `isSideNavExpanded`.
- When the rail collapses (`isSideNavExpanded === false`), we explicitly close any open submenu (`setIsExpanded(false)`).
- This guarantees that once your mouse leaves the rail (causing it to collapse), the dropdown no longer remains open on screen.
- We also added `useEffect` to the React import.
